RightToReply:
&lt;p&gt;
	I agree with the inspection results but have since carried out the following improvements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	The establishment has been thoroughly cleaned and procedures are in place to ensure that cleanliness is maintained.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	The establishment has been or will shortly be fully renovated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	A new management system has been implemented.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	The staff have been trained/re-trained/given instruction/are under revised supervisory arrangements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
	25/2/26 - I agree with the inspection results but have since carried out the following improvements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	&amp;middot;&amp;nbsp; The establishment has been thoroughly cleaned and procedures are in place to ensure that cleanliness is maintained.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	&amp;middot;&amp;nbsp; The establishment has been or will shortly be fully renovated.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	&amp;middot;&amp;nbsp; The staff have been trained/re-trained/given instruction/are under revised supervisory arrangements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	We appreciate the council&amp;rsquo;s visit and take food safety seriously. The sole point noted was a sink, which was installed immediately after. We were informed that with that fitted we would&amp;rsquo;ve been a clear 5 rating, all our food safety and hygiene procedures were spot on. However, we were told we must pay &amp;pound;180 for a rescore, which we feel is unfair. Instead, we chose to donate that amount to charity. We remain committed to best practices and disagree with the &amp;pound;180 fee the council request for our score that we deserve.&lt;/p&gt;
